course: dictionary
lesson: 3406
title: Explode: three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: The word explode means to burst apart with a loud bang and great force. «In 1970 an oxygen tank exploded on Apollo 13 on the way to the Moon.» The tank burst apart violently, so the word tells you something broke open with great force.
explain: Explode has two other meanings too. People can explode with anger, which means they suddenly become very angry, or explode with laughter, which means they suddenly laugh very loudly. Something can also explode by growing very fast, like a population exploding.
explain: To choose the right meaning, use the context. Ask what happened around the word, then swap in your meaning and check it still makes sense. If you read «Dad will explode if we forget the homework», the clue is that he is cross, not that he is about to burst apart.
fact: Explode is a verb: explode, explodes, exploded, exploding.
fact: «Explode» means to burst apart with a loud bang and great force.
fact: «Explode» can mean to suddenly become very angry, or to laugh very suddenly and loudly.
fact: «Explode» can also mean to grow very fast, like a population exploding.
fact: Aerosol cans, batteries and gas bottles can explode if they are heated, so keep them away from fire.
exercise: «In 1970 an oxygen tank exploded on Apollo 13.» What does exploded mean here? | Went quietly out of use | Slowly turned into a bright light show | *Burst apart with a loud bang and great force | Became very angry and shouted
exercise: «Ben tried not to explode with laughter in class.» What does explode mean here? | Go very quiet and still | *Laugh suddenly and very loudly | Burst into pieces | Fall fast asleep
exercise: Which thing should you keep away from fire because it can explode if heated? | A cup of cold water | A book about volcanoes | *A gas bottle or an aerosol can | Your pencil case
test: In «The population of the town exploded after the new factory opened», explode means: | Grew very fast | *Grew very fast, like a population | Burst apart with a bang | Fell down slowly
test: Which sentence uses explode to mean suddenly becoming very angry? | The balloon exploded with a bang. | *Dad will explode if we forget the homework again. | The tank exploded on the way to the Moon.
exam: Which meaning best fits «The crowd exploded with cheers when the goal went in»? | Fell silent and still | Burst apart into pieces | Grew very small and quiet | *Burst out suddenly with great excitement
